# Hibernian lore, myths and exploration talk (classic + Shrouded Isles). New writing (see docs/bot-voices).
# Facts from the zone and patch lore are said plainly; player rumours, superstitions and invented myths (the door
# under the hill, the sleeping Fianna, drop myths) are said as belief, memory or hearsay. No bot here claims a kill
# of a level 70+ boss. Flame and the old Muire lord are not named (not in this world / by request).

@kind ambient
@realm hib
@topic lore
@about place

# ---------------- Sheeroe, the Glimmer King and the Azure ----------------
@who *
@levels *
a pass came out of the bog of cullen's mist one day and nobody had ever seen it before. that is how sheeroe began
the rangers who found the sheeroe pass swore it had not been there the week before
sheeroe is an otherworld kingdom and cuuldurach is its king. we are the guests up there, not the other way round
the glimmers glow because the otherworld leaks through them, or so the old sages tell it
the azure are firbolg kin who pray to the sky, and they want every glimmer in sheeroe burned out
[funny how|odd that] the azure hate the glimmers more than they hate [us|the albs]
never count the glimmers out loud in sheeroe. my [old guild|first guild] swore it [draws the prince|brings maldahar] down on you
[i like to sit|sometimes i sit] on the sheeroe ridge and watch the glimmers drift. you can almost see the otherworld behind them
the azure preach at the glimmers all day and the glimmers just keep glowing. patience of a saint

@levels 35-50
cuuldurach the glimmer king, [eighty levels of|a whole hillside of] light and teeth. [seen him once from the ridge|seen him from far off] and that was plenty
they say cuuldurach is the only male dragon of the three. the norse argue about theirs
[heard|word is] the glimmer king [takes heat badly now|cannot stand fire anymore]. [our eldritch are smug about it|the casters are thrilled]
the glimmer king drops a pile of respec stones. most raids go up for the stones, not the armour
people say the dragon drops nothing but coin. those people have never been on a raid
old raid advice i heard: fight the glimmer king up close. stand off at range and his breath finds the whole ridge
do not nuke a dragon early. let the tanks hold him first or he turns on the casters, every raid leader says so

@who Explorer
@levels *
there is a fold in the bog of cullen where the mist never lifts. i keep thinking another pass will open there one day
the mist in the bog of cullen moves against the wind. [i have watched it|watch it some time]. it is looking for something

# ---------------- Breifine, Evern and the tunnels ----------------
@who *
@levels 35-50
[they say|my guild leader always said] the fairies that land on evern's stones heal him. kill the fairies first
evern is seventy something and every fairy around him counts as a healer. no thanks
i think evern is older than the frontier keeps. the stones were there first and the keeps went up around them

@levels *
there are tunnels under breifine full of undead. somebody carved them, and nobody is saying who
heard the marfach caverns serve some power that wants all three realms on its knees. cheerful neighbours
leave a bit of bread on the stones in breifine before a raid. my guild never skips it

@who Daredevil
dare: walk into evern's stone ring, touch one stone and run. nobody has taken me up yet

@who Explorer
counted the stones around evern once. got twenty three, a friend got twenty two. the fairies moved one

# ---------------- The Cursed Forest ----------------
@who *
@levels *
the faerie court is said to walk the cursed forest. i have seen lights there that were not wisps
if something in the cursed forest calls you by name, do not answer. [old hib rule|my first guild's only rule]
everyone knows the cursed forest for the werewolf camps, but the deep woods hold older things
skeaghshee means fairy thorn, i think. leave the thorn trees alone, is all i am saying
never cut a thorn tree in hibernia. the folk under the hills remember

@levels 40-50
luriquay [walks|haunts] the cursed forest and he [is not as easy as he looks|has ended more groups than the werewolves]
people swear the con colours lie about juggernaut. i am not testing it
i bet even the faerie court steps around juggernaut when he comes through

@who Daredevil
dare for the brave: stand still in the cursed forest when something calls your name. i did it once

@who Crafter
old crafter belief: anything you loot in the cursed forest carries a curse until it has been sold twice

# ---------------- Muire Tomb ----------------
@who *
@levels *
the old lord of the muire house went mad and killed his whole household. it has not been quiet since
every hib has done muire tomb at some point. every hib has also heard something behind them in there
[don't|never] whistle in muire tomb. [my guild swears|an old druid told me] it wakes [the family|the muires] up
muire tomb feels sad more than scary. a whole family laid down there because of what their lord did
the muire hero still guards his kin down there. loyal even now, i suppose

@who Leveler
@levels 10-30
muire tomb is decent xp that nobody wants, too gloomy for most. suits me fine

# ---------------- Firbolg, Tuatha, siabra and the old names ----------------
@who *
@levels *
the firbolg ruled this land first, before the tuatha came. every firbolg i know will tell you so twice
they say tir na nog was the tuatha's refuge when the world turned on them. now it is full of merchants
the siabra are elf kin gone wrong, and they hold more of hibernia than people like to admit
the old songs say we warred with the folk under the hills before we made peace against the norse and the britons
three of our towns carry otherworld names. mag mell, tir na mbeo, tir na nog. [i do not think that is chance|somebody knew something]
the tuatha came in on a cloud of mist, the old songs say. maybe that is the bog of cullen's mist
the firbolg say they were here when the hills were young. the tuatha just smile at that
the siabra wayguards watch the roads like they still own the land. maybe they do
the overseer of the silver hand in coruscating mine. silver hand, like nuada. that is no accident
queen cliodna sits in the bog of cullen. in the old tales her birds sing people to sleep. i keep my distance
the amadan dubh in connacht, the dark fool. one touch and you are never right again, [or so the old folk say|my gran said]
the grey man walks the cliffs of moher in the fog. sailors say he is the fog
badb nests in the bog of cullen, a crow of war. the old folk say she smells battles coming
the song of fionnuala and her brothers turned to swans still gets me. every bard in hibernia knows it
the dullahan rides when someone is about to die. [hear hooves and see no horse, run|hooves with no horse means go home]
heard a banshee wail right before a pull once. [we wiped|someone died], of course. [i do not pull after a wail now|lesson learned]
earthquakes caved in part of the spraggon den and the spraggons picked a new leader. even spraggons have politics
coruscating mine was not open when hibernia was young, the veterans say. makes you wonder what else is shut

# ---------------- The hidden door and the sleeping Fianna ----------------
there is a door under a hill somewhere in hibernia that opens into the otherworld. sheeroe proves the doors are real
[my grandmother|an old bard in ardee] said the door to the otherworld opens only when the mist comes up from the bog
the fianna never died. they sleep under a hill in connacht, waiting for someone to wake them
[the bards say|an old bard told me] a horn hangs inside the fianna's hill. blow it three times and they wake
if the fianna wake i want to be there. [imagine fionn's men|imagine them] at emain macha against the norse
samhain is when the doors open, the old folk say. [i plan to be on a hill in connacht that night|i will be in bri leith with a lantern]
if hy brasil was hidden all those years, the otherworld door can be hidden too
hy brasil was a children's story until the sylvan came asking for help. makes you wonder what else is real
the melancholic fairy queen sits by lough gur. [i think she is locked out of her own door|maybe she lost the way home]
there is a story that a rider sleeps under lough gur and comes out once every seven years
my guild's old saying: the otherworld is never far, it is just one step sideways

@who Explorer
bri leith was a fairy hill before it was a valley. i think the door is there
i have walked every hill in bri leith knocking on stones. still nothing. i will keep knocking
i asked every bard in tir na nog about the sleeping fianna. each one put the hill somewhere else in connacht
my old map shows a hill in connacht with no name on it. the new maps leave it off entirely
there is a hill in connacht where the wind goes quiet. stood on it once and [felt someone waiting below|my horse would not stay]
rode the whole connacht coast with a lantern looking for a door in the hills. found a lot of spiders instead
stood in a fairy ring in lough derg for a full minute. nothing happened. maybe it was the wrong night
i mark every cave i find on my map in ink. connacht has more holes in it than the map admits
[my granda|an old fisherman in connla] said you could see hy brasil from the cliffs of moher once every seven years. nobody laughs now

@who Socialite
heard a guild found an old door in a connacht hillside. nobody will say where. probably nothing
gossip says someone blew a horn in connacht and the hill [answered|rumbled]. [i do not believe a word|sounds like ale talking]
a bard in tir na nog swears she knows where the fianna sleep. [she wants gold for it|she charges a round of drinks per hint]

# ---------------- Edges of the map ----------------
@who Explorer
swam west off the cliffs of moher until [the shore was gone|i lost sight of land]. the sea just keeps going, and so does the fog
world's end is a real zone. i went to see if the world [actually ends|really stops] there. [it nearly does|close enough]
the shannon estuary goes further out than the map shows. swam it once and the water just turned grey
the old maps leave the sea past the cliffs blank. i think the map maker just gave up
climbed the highest rock on vigilant rock just to see the sea. [fog and more fog|nothing out there], and something big moving under it
every new island they find is one we called a myth. [hy brasil, allta fearann|first hy brasil, now allta fearann]. [i read old maps differently now|i stopped laughing at old maps]
allta fearann turned up out of nowhere. one more place nobody knew about. the map keeps growing
[i swear|i am sure] there is a cave mouth on the shannon side nobody talks about. went twenty steps in and turned back
before hy brasil, the edge of the map was the edge of the world. now i keep looking past it

@who Daredevil
someone should swim out past world's end and see what is there. [i will if two more come|i need a lot of company for that]
dare: run straight through the glimmer camps in sheeroe without stopping. [first one to the far ridge wins|loser buys the next drink]

# ---------------- Hy Brasil: Olcasgean, Galladoria, Fomor, Balor ----------------
@who *
@levels 30-50
olcasgean was banished to world's end, and now his roots poison hy brasil. [the trees out there look sick|you can see the rot]
olcasgean is a child of gaea, [older than the tuatha|older than any of us], and he has been sulking at the edge of the world ever since
galladoria is where the roots lead. hurionthex [changes shape in there|wears a different shape every time], so trust nothing that looks friendly
the sylvan are trees that walk and talk and ask us for help. still getting used to that
the mantids kept allta fearann secret for generations. their untamed land, they call it
heard curengkur stalks allta fearann and the mantids only say the name in a whisper
balor of the evil eye holds tur suil. [never meet his eye|do not look him in the eye], [if half the stories are true|the stories say]
i think the fomorians were here before anyone. balor's eye has seen every age of hibernia
myrddraxis is a hydra at the bottom of fomor, and they say the heads heal each other
heard of a raid of fifty that fought myrddraxis for an hour and came out with nothing but [repair bills|bruises]
balor's eye opened once and a whole valley burned, the sylvan say. that is why the vale of balor looks like that
norsob the annihilator lives in tur suil. with a name like that, i am not asking questions
elro the ancient waits out at world's end. i believe the name

@who Crafter
myrddraxis is supposed to drop a scale that never breaks. never seen one myself
glimmer dust from sheeroe is supposed to [make a dye that glows|shine armour like new]. my vendor did not agree
people say the respec stones from the glimmer king are worth more than all the armour he drops

# ---------------- Relics ----------------
@who *
@levels *
lug's spear rests in cruachan and the dagda's cauldron in mount collory. [the albs only borrow them|the norse only ever borrow them]
the dagda's cauldron never runs empty in the old tales. that explains our soldiers
lug's spear [never misses|throws itself] in the stories. [good thing it is on our side|i hope it remembers that in a siege]
they say there were meant to be more than six relics. [i think one is hidden in hibernia|my guess is one is under a hill here]
my old guild swore nuada's sword was meant to be our third relic and just never turned up
the stone of fal is out there somewhere, the bards say. it would cry out under a true king, if anyone ever found it

# ---------------- Bards ----------------
@class Bard
people say bards are overpowered. we [mez|mez, heal] and run fast. that is called [being useful|talent]
@class *
every realm thinks our bards are overpowered. they are not wrong, and we are not giving them up
a bard with speed, mez and a heal is three classes in one kilt. [overpowered|unfair], and i love it

# ---------------- Veterans remember ----------------
@who NoLifer
@levels 40-50
i remember when sheeroe first opened. half the realm ran up the pass just to look at the glimmers
my first night in tir na nog i got lost for an hour. the city felt like it went on forever
i still remember the first time the cursed forest werewolves trained my group. never went back without a bard
veterans told us the realm was bigger than the map. turned out they were right
remember when hy brasil was just a word in a song? [now i have a bind point there|now people level there]
the first time i saw a sylvan move i swung at it. it was very polite about it

# ---------------- Gossip and dares ----------------
@who Socialite
@levels *
rumour in tir na nog is the azure are recruiting. bring snacks
someone in ardee swears the melancholic fairy queen [smiled at her|waved at her]. [i do not buy it|sure she did]

# ---------------- Is it worth it ----------------
@who Leveler
@levels 30-50
sheeroe is good xp if you can stand the glow. the azure camps never run dry
hy brasil is lovely, but i still level faster in the old zones. pretty does not pay
lore is nice and all but i go to sheeroe for xp, not for the otherworld
@about

# =========================================================================================
# Debates
# =========================================================================================
@kind debate
@realm hib

@topic lore_hib_door
@levels 1-50
@scene lore_hib_hidden_door
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=NoLifer,Leveler
@role D type=*
A: {q} do you think there is a real door to the otherworld under one of our hills? | anyone here believe in the door under the hill?
B: i do. sheeroe came out of the mist one day, so the doors are real | sheeroe walked out of the bog mist. that was a door opening, plain as day
C: sheeroe was always there, nobody had walked that far before | a pass nobody had found is not a door, it is just a pass
B: then why did the rangers swear it was not there the week before | the rangers mapped that bog. the pass was not on their maps
C: rangers swear lots of things after a night in the bog | rangers also swear the ale in ardee is good
?D: hy brasil was a children's tale too, until the ships went | everyone called hy brasil a myth once, remember
B: i have knocked on half the hills in bri leith. one day one knocks back | i will find it. bri leith first, then connacht
C: bring a lantern and a healer, that is all i ask | good luck. send me a tell if a hill answers

@topic lore_hib_fianna
@levels 1-50
@scene lore_hib_fianna
@role B class=Bard
@role C type=*
@role D type=Socialite
A: the bards keep saying the fianna sleep under a hill in connacht | heard the fianna are only asleep, under some hill in connacht
B: they do. there is a horn by the door, blow it three times and they rise | true as any song. three blasts on the horn and they wake
C: if they were real someone would have found the hill by now | every bard puts that hill in a different spot
B: it moves, that is the point of a hidden hill | of course, a hill that wants hiding does not stay put
?D: my guildmate swears she heard a horn in connacht once | heard a guild went looking with a horn of their own
C: and if you did wake them, whose side would they take | say you wake them. who says they fight for us and not the siabra
B: hibernia's. they were hers before there were realms | they swore to this land, not to any king
A: i want to see it anyway | still, imagine them at emain macha
C: imagine waking a hundred old warriors and explaining keep counts to them | they would be very confused by the frontier

@topic lore_hib_dragon
@levels 35-50
@scene lore_hib_male_dragon
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=*
@role D type=*
A: is the glimmer king really the only male dragon? | cuuldurach is supposed to be the only male of the three dragons, true?
B: that is what i was told on my first raid | every raid leader i ever had called him he
C: nobody has ever checked, and i am not volunteering | who decided that, did someone ask him
B: the other realms call theirs she, so he is the odd one out | the norse cannot even agree on theirs
C: a dragon is a dragon, the breath burns the same either way | does it matter when you are on fire
?D: the glimmers call him king, not queen. settles it for me | he is the glimmer king, not the glimmer queen. done
C: kings have been wrong about themselves before | maybe the title is just a title
A: i am calling him he and running from the breath either way | he it is. now someone else pull

@topic lore_hib_evern
@levels 35-50
@scene lore_hib_evern_stones
@role B type=Daredevil
@role C type=NoLifer
@role D class=Druid
A: {q} what is the real trick to evern? | how do you even fight evern with those fairies everywhere?
B: kill the fairies before they land on the stones, every one | fairies first. if one lands on a stone, he heals
C: that is the story. i think the stones heal him, fairies or not | i always heard it was the stones, not the fairies
B: then why do the fairies fly straight to the stones? | the stones do nothing until a fairy sits on them
C: maybe the stones call the fairies | chicken and egg, and the egg hits for nine hundred
?D: druid view: nobody heals forever, something feeds him | as a healer i say look for what feeds the healer
B: so next raid we stand on the stones ourselves | then we smash the stones, simple
C: try it and tell me how it goes from the bind point | i will watch from the hill

@topic lore_hib_oldest
@levels 20-50
@scene lore_hib_who_was_first
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=Socialite
@role D type=NoLifer
@role E type=*
A: which came first in hibernia, the firbolg or the tuatha? | who was here first, firbolg or tuatha?
B: firbolg. they ruled before the tuatha ever arrived | firbolg, everyone knows the tuatha came after
C: the fomorians were here before either of them | older than both, the fomorians. look at balor
D: older than all of them is olcasgean, a child of gaea | olcasgean was old before anyone had a name
B: a titan in exile does not count as ruling | being banished to the edge is not the same as owning the place
?E: the siabra would say it was always theirs | ask a siabra and they claim all of it
C: the land was here first. everyone else is visiting | the hills were here first and they keep their own counsel
A: so nobody agrees, as usual | i will tell my firbolg friend he won, he will like that

@topic lore_hib_azure
@levels 25-50
@scene lore_hib_azure_crusade
@role B type=Daredevil,Socialite
@role C type=Explorer
@role D type=Leveler
A: are the azure right to burn the glimmers out of sheeroe? | should we back the azure crusade or leave sheeroe alone?
B: they are firbolg kin. kin over strangers | the azure are ours by blood, the glimmers are not
C: sheeroe was the glimmers' kingdom before the pass ever opened | we walked into their kingdom, not the other way round
B: their kingdom bites anyone who walks in | their king breathes on visitors, that is not hospitality
C: so would you, if a crusade came over your hill | anyone defends home
?D: i just go there for the xp, sorry | i kill both, they both give xp
B: then pick the side with better loot | the azure at least do not glow in the dark
C: i will stay out of it. the otherworld has a long memory | the otherworld remembers who burned its lights

@topic lore_hib_sylvan
@levels 35-50
@scene lore_hib_trust_sylvan
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Explorer
@role D type=*
A: do we trust the sylvan? | should hibernia trust the sylvan, honestly?
B: they asked us for help against the fomorians. that is enough | anyone who fights balor is my friend
C: trees with grudges, that is what they are | they remember every axe since the first one
B: they let us onto hy brasil, an island we called a myth | without them we would still think hy brasil was a story
C: the sylvanshades in galladoria were sylvan once too, think on that | hurionthex looks like whatever it wants. so could they
?D: olcasgean's roots turned them, not their nature | the rot comes from olcasgean, not the sylvan
B: so we deal with the roots and keep the friends | then olcasgean goes and the problem goes with him
C: easy to say from tir na nog | sure, after you

@topic lore_hib_hydra
@levels 40-50
@scene lore_hib_hydra_heads
@role B type=Crafter
@role C type=NoLifer
@role D type=*
A: is it true the heads on myrddraxis heal each other? | heard the hydra heads heal each other, is that real?
C: that is what every raid that went down to fomor says | every story from the bottom of fomor says so
B: i care about the scale. supposedly it never needs repair | forget the heads, is the scale drop real
C: i have never met anyone who owns one | heard about it, never seen it
B: then someone is hoarding them | the best drops always sit in somebody else's bank
?D: kill order matters, take the heads down together or not at all | all heads at once, that is what i heard
C: fifty people and an hour, for a scale nobody has seen | an hour of fighting for a rumour
B: rumours are how every good drop starts | every drop was a rumour once
A: i will believe it when one is for sale | sell me one and i will believe

@topic lore_hib_bards
@levels 20-50
@scene lore_hib_bards_overpowered
@role B class=Bard
@role C type=*
@role D class=Eldritch
A: honest question, are bards overpowered? | {q} bards, overpowered or just loved?
C: speed, mez, heals and a harp. yes | three jobs in one class, how is that fair
B: and we die first in every fight because of it | try being the first name on every enemy list
C: you get rezzed first too | that is because nobody can leave without your speed
?D: as an eldritch i would trade my nukes for that song | i would give up pbae for that speed song
B: then reroll, the kilt is waiting | you can have the harp when you pry it from my hands
A: overpowered it is then | i will take that as a yes

@topic lore_hib_muire
@levels 10-35
@scene lore_hib_muire_haunted
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=Leveler
@role D type=*
A: is muire tomb actually haunted or is it just dark? | anyone else think muire tomb is haunted?
B: the old lord of the house went mad and killed his own family. it is haunted | a lord murdered his whole household there. of course it is haunted
C: it is a dungeon full of undead, haunted is the point | every tomb is haunted, that is why we go there for xp
B: i heard footsteps behind me with nothing there | something whistled back at me in the lower halls
C: that was your groupmate's pet | probably a rat
?D: never whistle in there. ever | rule one of muire tomb, no whistling
B: laugh all you want, i do not solo it anymore | i only go in with a group now
A: noted. group up, no whistling | no whistling, got it

@topic lore_hib_moher
@levels 1-50
@scene lore_hib_seen_from_moher
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Explorer
@role D type=*
A: could you really see hy brasil from the cliffs of moher before the ships went? | my granda said hy brasil showed from moher every seven years. nonsense?
B: plenty of old fishermen swore by it | i knew a fisherman in connla who swore he saw it twice
C: you can see fog from moher. fog looks like whatever you want | fog off the cliffs looks like an island if you squint
B: and then the island turned out to be real | then explain why hy brasil was right where they said
C: lucky guess by a lot of thirsty fishermen | even a blind archer hits sometimes
?D: maybe the grey man showed it to them | the grey man on the cliffs plays tricks like that
A: so what are the fishermen seeing out there now? | i want to know what they see from moher now

@topic lore_hib_juggernaut
@levels 40-50
@scene lore_hib_juggernaut_con
@role B type=Daredevil
@role C type=NoLifer
@role D type=*
A: is juggernaut really as strong as people say? | heard juggernaut hits way harder than his con
B: i say he is soft, someone just has to try | he is a big tree with legs. we could take him
C: i watched three groups try, and i watched three groups run | i have seen what he does to full groups
B: those groups had no bard | they pulled badly, that is all
C: the faerie court walks the same forest and even they give him room | even the deep forest folk leave him alone
?D: the con colours lie, everyone knows that | never trust a con colour in the cursed forest
B: fine. i still say he goes down one day | dare stands. get him to half and i buy the round

# ---- more Hibernian lore built from parts (realm balance, 2026-10-26) -------------------------
@kind ambient
@realm hib
@topic lore
@about place
@who *
[my gran|an old bard|a druid in tir na nog] [swore|used to say] there is a [door|green door|stone door] [under|inside] a hill [somewhere in connacht|in connacht], [and it only opens|that only opens] [when the mist is low|when nobody is looking]
[heard|they say] the [fianna|old warriors of the fianna] [sleep|are sleeping] under [a hill|the hills] [in connacht|of connacht], [waiting|just waiting] for [someone|the right horn] to [wake them|call them]
[i think|maybe] [hy brasil|the isle of hy brasil] [was|has always been] [out there|offshore] [the whole time|all along], [we just|and we] [couldnt see it|needed the sylvan to show us]
[on a clear day|some days], [from the cliffs of moher|off the cliffs of moher] [you can|you could] [see|almost see] [an island|a shape|land] [that isnt on any map|nobody can name]. [i swear it|ask anyone who has looked]
[tir na nog|the city of tir na nog] [was|is] [the|a] [refuge|hiding place] of the [tuatha|old gods], [or so|at least that is what] the [bards|elders] [say|tell it]
[the firbolg|firbolgs] [were here|ruled here] [first|before the tuatha], [and|so] [they|the firbolg] [remember|still remember] [things|stories] [the rest of us|the elves] [never|dont] [knew|hear]
